{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.635639Z","id":"b3c82417f8f48a4c10565c34a9587b107ccb58b0a9f2ff5d40553907563e9f94","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/views/thread.rs:944-988, record da32124b.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1569-1613, record e7b6d312.\n\nSpec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":944},"end":{"line":988},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
